ate is $17.50 for 0 - 1,500 gallons. All wastewater over the monthly minimum is $5.75 per 750 gallons. | This is how the sewer rates are calculated: the first year at a new residence, or for all commercial c", "is for residential usage is recalculated every year based upon the usage in October and November and takes effect on each January's billing. | Storm Water | Residential storm water utility rates are billed a flat fee of $6.00. Proceeds from this federally mandated utility goes toward the city's storm water replacement fund. | | EPA Compliance Fee: Billed a monthly flat rate of $15.00 per residential. | | Trash: Trash", "idential storm water utility rates are billed a flat fee of $6.00. Proceeds from this federally mandated utility goes toward the city's storm water replacement fund. | | EPA Compliance Fee: Billed a monthly flat rate of $15.00 per residential. | | Trash: Trash is picked up once per week for a flat fee of $18.00 per month. The City has several sizes of poly-carts available for rent from the City at $2.00 per month. Ma", "nce Fee: Billed a monthly flat rate of $15.00 per residential. | | Trash: Trash is picked up once per week for a flat fee of $18.00 per month. The City has several sizes of poly-carts available for rent from the City at $2.00 per month. Make sure your trash is available for pickup no later than 6 a.m. on your scheduled day. For individuals needing assistance, a walk-in sanitation service is available for $21.00 per m", "lable for rent from the City at $2.00 per month. Make sure your trash is available for pickup no later than 6 a.m. on your scheduled day. For individuals needing assistance, a walk-in sanitation service is available for $21.00 per month. | Monday- Bulk Trash (all Wards) | Tuesday-Third Ward | Wednesday-Fourth Ward | Thursday-First Ward | Friday-Second Ward | How Can We Serve You? | Submit Questions or Comments Contac"], "via": "Utility Rates"}]}
