{"id": 2178, "name": "Napawalla Park (Oxford)", "read": "2026-10-15", "pages": [{"url": "https://oxfordks.org/Community/Parks", "lines": ["enches with plenty of shade from surrounding trees makes this a great spot to bring kids. | | | Cave Park has five different pavilions that can be reserved by contacting the City Office. The fee to reserve a pavilion is $5.00 per day with payment due at the time of reservation | | Napawalla Camping Fees: | $15.00 Electric Hook Up $3.50 Primitive PER DAY | Campsites are first come first serve, the city DOES NOT take r", "rge swing set, a toddler swing set, a merry-go-round, spring riders and the large play structure for children of all ages to enjoy! | | Both Primitive and RV camping are available at Napawalla Park. Primitive camping is $3.50 per day and Electric hook up is $15.00 per day. The \"self-pay\" station for payment of camping fees is located at the north end of the park. Water is available throughout the park and a sewer dum", " the City Office if you have questions about their current status. | | There are two shelters in the park that can be reserved by contacting the City Office. This is a first-come, first-serve policy and reservations are $5.00 per day, with payment due at the time of reservation. | | The park has a horse shoe pit, it's even lit at night so you can play horseshoes even after dark. | | Sand Volleyball is also available "]}, {"url": "https://oxfordks.org/Government/Comprehensive-Fee-Schedule", "lines": [], "via": "Comprehensive Fee Schedule"}, {"url": "https://oxfordks.org/Community/Watermelon-Feed", "lines": [], "via": "Watermelon Feed"}]}
